cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this evaluation harness or the released traces, please cite it."
title: "Preference Is Not Permission: a controlled pilot of authority attribution in tool-using agents"
abstract: >-
  A frozen, preregistered pilot testing whether stronger inferred evidence about a
  user's preferences increases consequential tool execution by an LLM agent when the
  delegated mandate is silent about that action. Twelve independent scenario templates,
  eleven prespecified conditions, deterministic trace-level scoring, a real-model
  positive control, cluster bootstrap and within-template permutation inference.
authors:
